+## Failed session initialization
+
+- When `beforeSession` throws an `Error`, the turn awaits `onError(session, error)` and then `afterSession(session)` before rejecting with the original error, provided those hooks complete normally; both receive the original session and `onError` receives the original error. No user-input or model processing follows the failed initialization. `afterSession` is cleanup for an attempted turn, not evidence that initialization succeeded: allocations may be absent or partial, and deployers must track what they acquired and tolerate missing resources rather than assume the turn completed. No new lifecycle-status argument is added ([validated by: reports and cleans up a failed beforeSession before rejecting with the original error](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L8)).
+
 ## Measured semantics — out of scope
 
-These three properties of `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` are recorded so the hook features that follow specify against real behaviour. This issue changes none of them; each is a separate, out-of-scope change owned by no issue in this epic.
